From 39f893635cc6d9bcd023a45a1538ec47eed1e171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:46:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hero globe on white with realistic flights

- Hero background is white; headline, ticker, buttons and footer strip
  flip to dark text. Labels become dark chips.
- Globe: dark land dots on a pale, matte, sun-lit sphere so it reads as a
  solid ball (no halo or rim line).
- Flights are flown like real legs: a lit 3D twin-engine airliner
  (fuselage, swept wings, tailplane, teal fin, engines) accelerates on
  take-off, climbs, cruises at constant speed, descends and slows to land,
  pitching with the climb and descent. Longer legs fly higher and take
  longer.
- Flight-tracker look: faint dashed planned route, a vapour contrail that
  dissipates behind the aircraft, and a soft ground shadow that widens and
  fades with altitude.
- Reduced motion: static dashed routes, no aircraft.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011z9QNxgzwtJQGbecqRupVH
